    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0282" n="232" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg232"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/375</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d367-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-05-02T12:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 2, 1918,
                                noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 30, 2 p.m.,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d367-f2"/> also telegram April 29, 4
                        p.m.,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d367-f3"/> from Harbin, in which Consul reports
                    that Semenov desires American railway
                    engineers under Stevens to take over
                    operation of all railways <pb facs="0283" n="233" xml:id="pg233"/> behind him,
                    apparently with view to facilitating passage of supplies for his forces and also
                    for civil population back of his lines which is in great need.</p>
                <p>Inform Stevens that the Russian Railway
                    Service Corps was organized at the request of the Provisional Government of
                    Russia to assist in the reorganization of Russian railways and to help Russia as
                    a whole, and to enable the people to strengthen their resistance against
                    Germany. It is consequently impossible to permit this corps of American
                    engineers to be drawn in to take sides in a movement which partakes of civil
                    war, consequently their work on the Chinese Eastern Railway must not have any
                    semblance of supporting Semenov or
                    contributing to the success of his military operations. If this can only be
                    accomplished by their withdrawal then they should be withdrawn and the
                    Department will instruct Stevens as to
                    their further movements.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d367-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d367-f1-content">
                <p>The same information telegraphed, on the same date, to the Ambassador in Russia
                    (No. 102).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d367-f2" n="2" xml:id="d367-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="frus1918Russiav02#pg_147">Vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>,
